            <ArticleTitle>Extensor coxae brevis: treatment strategies for the deep lateral rotators in pelvic tilt.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>262-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jbmt.2009.12.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The group of myofascial units known as the deep lateral rotators are considered in light of their role as postural hip extensors, resulting functional and palpatory assessments of pelvic neutral are presented, and treatment strategies for anterior and posterior pelvic tilt are discussed.</AbstractText>
